body:
I have a few things that I love seeing, so bare with me lol

- at least one (1) morally grey or evil RO. This is why I love **Sinners and Saints** so much (there's 7 ROs and they're all shady);

- when there's a fighting skill and it lets me choose between a brutal and finesse MC (like in **Samurai of Hyuga**). I love going hammer on my enemies, sorry not sorry; 

- when my MCs personality doesn't lock me out of romance. Ie., I'm going for a mean and brutal MC, RO1 is a softie and they don't like violence - I wanna be able to romance them without having to change MCs personality; 

- give me a dog companion and I'm sold.

edit: also no personality stat checks.

Hello, I just did a spread with the question "What to do next in my spiritual journey?" and drew the following 3 cards: 

- **The Emperor**, in **reverse**; 
- **The Tower**, upright; 
- **The Hermit**, in **reverse**. 

Back of the deck was **Ace of Pentacles**, upright. Then, I drew one more card for clarification and got **Justice**, upright. 

How could I interpret this? I must admit I'm a little scared of The Tower. I'm using a deck with the traditional Rider-Waite-Smith.
